{"requests": [
 {"kind": "fits", "text": "ok so I just wrapped a 4-month ADK build for a regional insurer and I keep forgetting stuff between gigs. can you help me start a personal notes thing (NOT in the repo, the client owns that) where I capture who they are: claims + underwriting business, the state insurance regs they kept bringing up, who the actual decision makers were vs the loud ones, PII/PHI they hold, their GCP setup (Vertex, BigQuery, VPC-SC everywhere), and what went wrong with our eval pipeline. Just interview me, I'll answer. Next engagement starts Monday and I want you to be able to pull this up later."},
 {"kind": "fits", "text": "I have a folder of old SOWs, kickoff decks and retro docs from three previous clients (~/Documents/clients). Can you import those into some kind of per-client profile kept outside any project dir, so in future sessions you already know each org's stack, compliance constraints, stakeholders and lessons learned? Also want to be able to look over what you extracted, fix wrong bits, and export a client's profile to markdown if I need to hand it to a colleague."},
 {"kind": "elsewhere", "text": "Our ADK agent for the retail client needs to remember each shopper's preferences and past orders across sessions. Right now it forgets everything when the session ends. We're on Cloud Run with Firestore available. How do I wire this up properly? Demo is Thursday.", "needs_instead": "Implementing persistent long-term memory inside the ADK agent itself (e.g. a MemoryService / session service backed by Firestore or Vertex AI Memory Bank) for end users, not a personal knowledge base about the developer's clients."}
]}
